# Per-machine affordance recorder log. HARNESS.md declares this LOCAL
# (per-machine only) — session invocation noise, not project state.
observability/affordance-invocations.json

# Probe environment. The pre-Phase-0 probe (PRD §9) is throwaway by
# instruction; its venv is not a project artefact. Phase 0 introduces a real
# pyproject.toml.
.venv/

# Voice recordings — deliberately never committed.
#
# This is a public repository. A voice recording is not something you can
# unpublish: once cloned, cached and indexed, it is out. The Phase 1 engine
# benchmark (PRD §2, accuracy-measurement note) needs a desk-mic corpus so
# YOUR results are reproducible by you — it does not need strangers to be
# able to replay your voice.
#
# To regenerate the corpus on a new machine, record ~10s of natural dictation
# per sample at 16 kHz mono 16-bit PCM:
#
#   ffmpeg -f avfoundation -list_devices true -i ""      # find your mic index
#   ffmpeg -f avfoundation -i ":0" -t 10 -ar 16000 -ac 1 \
#          -c:a pcm_s16le tests/fixtures/asr/sample-01.wav
#
# Use the mic you actually dictate with. A Bluetooth headset has a different
# acoustic profile from a desk mic, and a corpus recorded on one measures that
# one — PRD §2 specifies desk-mic English.
#
# Reference transcripts (*.txt) ARE committed: they carry no voice, and WER is
# meaningless without them.
tests/fixtures/asr/*.wav
tests/fixtures/asr/*.m4a
# Spontaneous-speech corpus (scripts/record_spontaneous.py). Same rule, and it
# needs no reference transcripts at all — the questions it answers are
# "do disfluencies survive the decoder" and "what does trimming actually
# remove", neither of which is a WER question.
tests/fixtures/spontaneous/
# No trailing slash, deliberately. The slashed form matches a directory and
# NOT a symlink of the same name — and a symlink is exactly what a worktree
# uses to reach the corpus in the lobby checkout, so the slashed pattern let
# a path to a voice recording into a commit on 2026-08-08. A symlink carries
# no audio, but the rule this file exists to enforce is that nothing about a
# voice recording reaches a public repository, and a path is something.
tests/fixtures/spontaneous
tests/fixtures/phase3/
tests/fixtures/phase3
# NOT `tests/fixtures/asr` bare — that directory holds the committed reference
# transcripts, and WER is meaningless without them. Only its audio is ignored.
tests/fixtures/asr/*.flac
probe.wav

# Local voice recordings (see note above). Never committed.
.audio/

# macOS directory metadata
.DS_Store

# Python build and tool artefacts. None of these are project state; all are
# regenerable from pyproject.toml and the source tree.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Per-experiment virtualenvs (Track 2). Each experiment gets its own so that
# concurrent installs cannot collide; none of them is a project artefact.
.venv-*/

# The tier-check reference clip (PRD §7.2). Generated by
# scripts/make_tier_clip.sh, not committed: it is macOS `say` output and the
# redistribution grant for a system TTS voice is not clear. §7.2 calls for a
# clip "shipped with the app", so this has to be settled before Phase 4
# packages anything — see docs/gates/phase-1.md.
src/amanuensis/assets/*.wav

# The landing page's JavaScript toolchain (SITE_PRD §11). Regenerable from
# site/package-lock.json; neither is project state.
site/node_modules/
site/dist/
site/.astro/

# SQLite sidecars the site fixture generator leaves behind. The fixture itself
# is committed; its write-ahead log is not project state and differs on every
# run even when the exported output is byte-identical.
tests/fixtures/site/*.db-wal
tests/fixtures/site/*.db-shm
tests/fixtures/site/history.db
